James sought insights about key individuals scheduled for a department visit centered around climate economics and innovation. The discussion included notable attendees like **Jeffrey Sun**, the organizer; **Jacquelyn Pless**, focused on energy and clean technology; **Christian Spielmann**, an applied economist; and **Karen Clay**, an expert in economic history related to environmental issues. I provided talking points and conversation hooks for effectively engaging each participant, emphasizing the importance of addressing economic disparities concerning climate impacts. Strategies for the seminar included highlighting the relevance of GDP impacts while acknowledging welfare limitations and exploring the implications of the meta-analysis for inequality. Recommendations emphasized deeper discussions with senior scholars like Clay and Souza-Rodrigues, while fostering dialogue with junior attendees on methodological critiques and pressing climate-economy questions.
